{
  "$schema": "./SCHEMA.md#self-certifying-tree-head",
  "description": "Verification of a tree head of a self-certifying node:<sha256-of-key> shard. The shard id is 'node:' plus the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the raw 32-byte Ed25519 public key that signs its heads, so a verifier handed a head and that key (the optional signing_public_key on GET /ledger/sth/latest and /ledger/sth/{tree_size}, outside the signed bytes) checks the key against the id and the head against the key, with no registry and no trust anchor. Checks run in this order and the first failure is reported: id is not a valid node: id (not_self_certifying), no key presented (missing_key), key is not exactly 64 lowercase hex characters decoding to a valid Ed25519 point (malformed_key), sha256 of the key bytes does not equal the id's hash (key_id_mismatch), signature does not verify over the standard Signed Tree Head signing bytes (bad_signature). expected.check names which verification applies to the shard id: self_certifying for a valid node: id, core_network for core (the existing network and witness verification, not exercised here), unsupported for every other id kind and every malformed id, which never verifies.",
  "supportedIn": [
    "rust",
    "csharp",
    "typescript"
  ],
  "generation": "Deterministic. signingKeySeedHex and otherKeySeedHex are the Ed25519 seeds of the two keys (signingPublicKeyHex / otherPublicKeyHex, ids selfCertifyingId / otherSelfCertifyingId). Each head's signatureHex is Ed25519 over the Signed Tree Head signing message (see signed-tree-head.json) of that head's own fields, produced with avalon_protocol::sth::sign_tree_head; 'signed by a different key' vectors use the other seed, and tampered vectors reuse the original signature with one field changed. The non-curve key is 0x01 0x7f followed by zeros, which fails point decompression. Never real credentials.",
  "signingKeySeedHex": "1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111",
  "signingPublicKeyHex": "d04ab232742bb4ab3a1368bd4615e4e6d0224ab71a016baf8520a332c9778737",
